  "notes": "The video-opening montage and an early stretch of commentary are identical, word for word, to a shorter July 2003 post titled \"Master of the Ring VII - PART ONE,\" which breaks off mid-tournament promising a delayed second part; \"The Supreme\" is the one complete version served here. The broadcast opens with a sixth Master of the Ring title match settling the prior tournament's own dispute, and runs a Tanning Bed Deathmatch, a six-man Pentagon Pain match, and a SuperBout brawl alongside the seventh tournament's own sixteen-man bracket. The fed's own retirement post (29 November 2003, not served) independently confirms the tournament's own final bracket results in prose; see this wing's own holdings list.",
